"""Independent 2038/A-C solutions."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ANSWERS=[
('2038/A','Engineer i will work at most floor(a[i]/b[i]) units without negative benefit. If total capacities are below k all choose zero because completion is impossible. Otherwise each engineer minimizes personal effort by leaving as much work as possible to later engineers: c[i]=max(0,remaining-totalLaterCapacity). This is within their capacity by feasibility and is the unique backward-induction optimum. O(n) time and space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;using ll=long long;int main(){int n;ll k;cin>>n>>k;vector<ll>a(n),cap(n),s(n+1);for(auto&x:a)cin>>x;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){ll b;cin>>b;cap[i]=a[i]/b;}for(int i=n-1;i>=0;i--)s[i]=s[i+1]+cap[i];if(s[0]<k){for(int i=0;i<n;i++)cout<<0<<' ';cout<<'\n';return 0;}for(int i=0;i<n;i++){ll c=max(0LL,k-s[i+1]);cout<<c<<' ';k-=c;}cout<<'\n';}'''),
('2038/B','Let x[i] count operations at i and h be the common final value. Equations are 2*x[i]-x[i-1]=a[i]-h. Put b[i]=x[i]+h, giving 2*b[i]-b[i-1]=a[i], independent of h, and a unique rational cyclic solution. Recover its integer candidate by iterating the monotone contracted map b[i]=floor((a[i]+b[i-1])/2), starting the cyclic predecessor at max(a). The largest floor fixed point equals the true solution when integral. At stabilization check every equation exactly; if any fails no integer solution exists. Otherwise maximize h subject to x[i]>=0 by h=min(b), and answer sum(a)-n*h. The contraction halves error per element, so O(n log max(a)) conservative time, O(n) space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;using ll=long long;int main(){ios::sync_with_stdio(false);cin.tie(nullptr);int t;cin>>t;while(t--){int n;cin>>n;vector<ll>a(n),b(n);ll sum=0,start=0;for(auto&x:a){cin>>x;sum+=x;start=max(start,x);}while(true){ll cur=start;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){cur=(a[i]+cur)/2;b[i]=cur;}if(cur==start)break;start=cur;}bool ok=true;ll prev=b.back(),h=LLONG_MAX;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){if(2*b[i]-prev!=a[i])ok=false;prev=b[i];h=min(h,b[i]);}cout<<(ok?sum-n*h:-1)<<'\n';}}'''),
('2038/C','Each of the four coordinate values consumes two copies, so sort and collect one token for each available equal pair. At least four tokens are necessary and sufficient. Choose the two smallest and two largest tokens a<=b<=c<=d. Any inner token can be moved outward to one of these extremes without hurting an optimal product. The optimal pairing is sides c-a and d-b: its product exceeds (d-a)*(c-b) by (b-a)*(d-c), and the disjoint pairing is no better. Output corners (a,b),(a,d),(c,b),(c,d). O(n log n) time, O(n) space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;using ll=long long;int main(){ios::sync_with_stdio(false);cin.tie(nullptr);int t;cin>>t;while(t--){int n;cin>>n;vector<ll>a(n),v;for(auto&x:a)cin>>x;sort(a.begin(),a.end());for(int i=0;i+1<n;i++)if(a[i]==a[i+1]){v.push_back(a[i]);i++;}if(v.size()<4){cout<<"NO\n";continue;}ll x=v[0],y=v[1],X=v[v.size()-2],Y=v.back();cout<<"YES\n"<<x<<' '<<y<<' '<<x<<' '<<Y<<' '<<X<<' '<<y<<' '<<X<<' '<<Y<<'\n';}}''')]
if __name__=='__main__':
    p=Path('backend/data/bench/codeforces700_20261116/assistant_answers_v1/shard_test_000_199.jsonl')
    with p.open('a',encoding='utf-8') as out:
        for ident,explanation,code in ANSWERS:
            out.write(json.dumps({'id':ident,'split':'test','author':'current chat assistant','status':'authored','explanation':explanation,'cpp_code':code,'validation':'not executed'})+'\n')
